#
# The palette as a Qt colour scheme (ERGON-139): twenty-one #AARRGGBB values per
# state, in QPalette::ColorRole order -- WindowText, Button, Light, Midlight,
# Dark, Mid, Text, BrightText, ButtonText, Base, Window, Shadow, Highlight,
# HighlightedText, Link, LinkVisited, AlternateBase, (NoRole), ToolTipBase,
# ToolTipText, PlaceholderText. qt5ct's own schemes have exactly this many; a
# short or long line is not an error, the palette is just wrong.
# Window is the desktop's background, Button and Base are one step up and
# AlternateBase two, the way gtk/gtk.css.in layers them.
